.TH COLORADO 1 "2026-08-16" "notcoreutils" "notcoreutils Manual"
.SH NAME
colorado \- generic stdin colorizer
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIcmd\fR | \fBcolorado\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B colorado
colorizes stdin: log\-level words, quoted strings, IPv4 addresses,
and numbers get ANSI colors (the same idea as
.BR grc (1)
or ccze, not a config\-file\-driven rule engine \- a fixed set of
common patterns). Everything else passes through unchanged, so
piping any command's output through
.B colorado
is always safe even on output it does not recognize.
